 *
 * Render surface where the centring offset is NOT half the render
 * width: 400x250 scales x4 to 1600x1000 at +160+140, so off_x is 160
 * while half the width is 200. At 320x200 and 640x400 the two happen
 * to be equal, which is what disguised a rotation by off_x as a
 * rotation by half the width. Keep this case in any scaler bisect.
 * Build with:
 *   west build ... -- -DEXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE=render-400x250.overlay
 */

&display {
	render-width = <400>;
	render-height = <250>;
};
